        "original_id": "11d4c226-4df2-5d77-8023-29cab1fd1c94",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hindmarsh Stadium, Adelaide, South Australia, Semaphore Park\n- Companies: Coopers Brewery\n- Organizations: Adelaide United FC\n- Parks and Landmarks: Fort Glanville Conservation Park, Fort Glanville\n\nFacts:\n- Hindmarsh Stadium is a multi-purpose stadium in Adelaide, South Australia.\n- Hindmarsh Stadium is currently known as Coopers Stadium because of sponsorship from the Adelaide-based Coopers Brewery.\n- Adelaide United FC's home ground is Hindmarsh Stadium.\n- In the 2013 financial year, Coopers Brewery sold 69.7 million litres of beer.\n- Fort Glanville Conservation Park is a protected area in Semaphore Park, a seaside suburb of Adelaide in South Australia.\n- Fort Glanville Conservation Park includes the functional 19th-century Fort Glanville and adjoining land.\n- Fort Glanville is listed on the South Australian Heritage Register.",
